; The band's own host and the names that follow from it agree (QUUX's
; Ethernet contract, sections 5.6 and 8, step R3; sys/network/host.lisp,
; SET-LOCAL-HOST-VARIABLES's cold initialization, and
; sys/network/ip/servers.lisp, INTERNET-SET-LOCAL-HOST).  Until they were set
; together, SI:LOCAL-HOST-NAME kept the saved band's host while SI:LOCAL-HOST
; was this boot's: on revision 16, "UNKNOWN-NIL-NIL" against
; "UNKNOWN-INTERNET-<address>".  On revision 15, with no network to drive a
; session, type the first form at the console.
(string= si:local-host-name (send si:local-host :name)) => T
; recorded: the host, its names, its location and the associated machine
(list (send si:local-host :name) si:local-pretty-host-name si:local-finger-location (send si:associated-machine :name))
